{{!-- Existing + add-new Specializations for one skill row, shared by skill-picker.hbs's two
     {{#each}} loops (real-Essence skills and "any"-Essence skills). Adding AND removing a
     Specialization both live here now, not on the actor sheet's own essence-skills.hbs (which is
     roll-only display) - see essence20-specialization-redesign. Initiative has no
     Specializations per every sourcebook - skip the whole block rather than render a dead
     control (Conditioning never reaches here at all - it isn't a system.skills entry). Also
     skipped for a still-untrained (d20) skill - every sourcebook requires at least a d2 Rank
     before a Specialization can be assigned ("You choose a skill in which you possess at least a
     d2 Rank and assign a Specialization to that skill"), so there's nothing valid to add yet. --}}
{{#unless (or (eq key 'initiative') (eq fields.shift 'd20'))}}
<div class="skill-picker-specializations">
  {{#each fields.specializations as |specialization specializationKey|}}
  <span class="chip skill-picker-specialization-chip">
    {{specialization.name}}
    {{#if specialization.granted}}<i class="fas fa-lock" data-tooltip="{{localize 'E20.SpecializationGranted'}}"></i>{{/if}}
    <a data-action="removeSpecialization" data-skill="{{../key}}" data-specialization-key="{{specializationKey}}" data-tooltip="{{localize 'E20.ItemControlDelete'}}">
      <i class="fas fa-xmark"></i>
    </a>
  </span>
  {{/each}}

  <div class="skill-picker-add-specialization" data-skill="{{key}}">
    {{!-- Every sourcebook is explicit its own list is suggestions, not a fixed catalog - the
         trailing "Custom..." option (which reveals the free-text input beside it) is always
         available, even for a skill/version with no standard list of its own. --}}
    {{!-- The leading placeholder is disabled so it reads as an instruction, not a real choice -
         the browser won't let the user navigate back to it once something else is picked, and
         skill-picker.mjs resets the select to it (index 0) after each add rather than leaving a
         stale real name showing. Its "" value is also how skill-picker.mjs tells "nothing chosen
         yet" apart from "Custom…" actually chosen - Custom now uses the CUSTOM_SPECIALIZATION_VALUE
         sentinel instead of "" for exactly that reason (see that file's own comment on it). --}}
    <select class="skill-picker-specialization-select">
      <option value="" disabled selected>{{localize 'E20.SpecializationChoosePlaceholder'}}</option>
      {{#each (lookup @root.standardSpecializations key) as |name|}}
      <option value="{{name}}">{{name}}</option>
      {{/each}}
      <option value="__custom__">{{localize 'E20.SpecializationCustomOption'}}</option>
    </select>
    <input type="text" class="skill-picker-specialization-custom" placeholder="{{localize 'E20.SpecializationCustomPlaceholder'}}" />
    <a data-action="addSpecialization" data-skill="{{key}}" data-tooltip="{{localize 'E20.AddSpecialization'}}">
      <i class="fas fa-plus"></i>
    </a>
  </div>
</div>
{{/unless}}
